ZERO OS 0.8.0 WINDOW MANAGER VM VERIFICATION
Date: 2026-11-16 UTC

FINAL TESTED ISO
SHA256:216bc7216b623240ca3cfb1e719139ac037d8c801a6cb44ee91b401a6692f651
Bytes:17645568. All six VM runs used this exact ISO and verified it unchanged.

FOUR-MODE MATRIX
BIOS x86-64: PASS,137 recorded actions,344 available slots.
BIOS x86-32 (-lm,-pae): PASS,94 recorded actions,344 available slots.
UEFI x86-64: PASS,94 recorded actions,88 available slots.
UEFI x86-32 (-lm): PASS,94 recorded actions,88 available slots.
Counts include function keys and submission of preserved partial input.
The host sends actual emulated PS/2 keystrokes via QMP; no guest code or
memory writes are injected. Each VM attaches its own copied ZeroFS and MBR
fixture disks. Full SHA256 hashes remained unchanged in this matrix.

Verified in all four modes:
- Two initial sessions, stable IDs, default focus1; create at least6.
- Real F1 new, F2 close, F3 next, F4 previous and F5 layout controls.
- Both sessions retain incomplete write commands across F3/F4 switching;
  ALPHA-PENDING and BETA-PENDING execute only in the intended sessions.
- Per-window volume rootsA/B survive focus changes; new windows inherit root.
- Closing/reusing slot3 preserves the other sessions; a closed numeric ID
  is rejected before slot reuse.
- clear affects only its window. Window1's408x352 body pixel region is
  byte-identical before/after clearing window2; window2's body changes.
- Tile and scrolling layouts, keyboard toggles and textual commands work.
- Changes made while graphics is paused appear after resume, including the
  latest focus/layout and LATEST-UPDATE output.
- Malformed commands, out-of-range/closed IDs leave inventory unchanged.
- The last session cannot be closed by either API; an incomplete command
  also survives a refused F2 and executes correctly on explicit Enter.

Additional BIOS read-only memory oracles pause the VM briefly and dump its
actual loader-owned slots at0x130000. They independently verify saved input,
root metadata, unchanged neighboring rings after clear, and zeroed reused
slot history. BIOS64 fills the7168-byte ring past capacity and confirms old
text is evicted, newest text remains and all other sessions stay unchanged.
No memory-write debugging commands are used.

ACTUAL UART REGRESSION
bios64-uart: PASS,7 recorded actions, no data disks.
Uses a real bidirectional emulated COM1 socket. A pending write SENTINEL in
window2 survives UART window2 followed by CRLF from window1: its input and
history ring remain byte-identical, with no output until explicit Enter.
That Enter prints SENTINEL exactly once. UART window new followed by CRLF
creates exactly one fresh prompt; a following write executes exactly once.

CROSS-WINDOW FILESYSTEM INTEGRATION
bios64-files: PASS,27 shell commands, separate disposable writable copies.
Three sessions selectB:|ext4,C:|NTFS,D:|Btrfs. Each creates the same filename
wm08 with its own text, switches away/back, replaces the file and reads the
correct session-specific content. This exercises arguments/input located
outside the kernel arena and the shared filesystem command engine.
After VM exit, independent e2fsck -fn, ntfsfix -n and btrfs check --readonly
all return0. debugfs,ntfscat and btrfs restore extract byte-exact
B-session-updated,C-session-updated,D-session-updated respectively.
MBR/outer gaps and the unused private ZeroFS disk are unchanged.
ntfsfix is a limited consistency check, not Windows chkdsk.

SCREENSHOTS
Real final-ISO VM images, not static design previews:
bios64/desktop-tiles.png and bios64/desktop-scroll.png show a clean3-session
demonstration, using actual terminal/root/task commands with no disk writes.
All four boot modes also retain raw tile/scroll/clear/resume evidence.
Selected final images from all four modes were visually inspected.
Animation was disabled during screenshot equality tests to keep the caret
stable; caret animation itself is outside this focused VM matrix.

SCOPE AND ARTIFACTS
All six QEMU processes exited. Original user disks were never attached.
QEMU is external test infrastructure, not guest implementation. Native
VirtualBox and physical hardware were not tested. Sessions share one command
engine; this report does not claim protected processes or parallel commands.
candidate-50e1a74d contains earlier candidate evidence, not final-ISO proof.
Initial harness corrections involved host ATA readonly configuration and
waiting for actual typed echo; they were not guest defects. The separate
filesystem harness was corrected to expect the foreign-filesystem success
message rather than the ZeroFS message before its successful final run.
Distribute source scripts,JSON/text/serial logs and PNG screenshots only;
private-disk-*,*.partition,*.memory,*.ppm,vars.fd and sockets are private test
artifacts, not delivery disk images. The distribution image remains ISO.
